# FUTURE
Currently, **Diorite** is not very performant, nor was it complete. In the future, I plan on revisiting the project.
This involves reducing **Diorite** to just a C# API (with the core remaining in F# implementation).

Some things will change:
- Tokenization handled by the parser (parser will request the next token) - better error detection
- Optimize parser combinators to efficiently prune branches that are not possible (+ better DSL)
- Memory is not optimized and the naive approach of copying memory to maintain immutability was a stupid idea (mine)
- C# API is NOT optimzed at all, the `Ast` is a big issue with loads of type inference and membership checks, which adds
  overhead (probably make it lazy)
